# Every text file checks out with LF on every platform, so a Windows clone with the default
# core.autocrlf=true sees the same bytes the Linux/CI checkout does. This is a DEFINITION, not an
# enumeration of extensions: byte-size and byte-identity checks in this repo (lead_package.size vs
# tools/lead_package_sizes.json, the mirror parity in tools/validate.py) are line-ending sensitive,
# and pinning only *.py/*.sh/VERSION was exactly BUG-0025 -- a CRLF checkout inflated the lead
# instruction package (.md) past its recorded size and install.sh's validate step aborted before it
# installed any hook. `eol=lf` overrides core.autocrlf, so the working tree no longer depends on it.
# (The kit content hash normalizes CRLF itself -- kernel.hashing.kit_hash -- so it is unaffected
# either way; the size check is the one that reads raw on-disk bytes.)
* text=auto eol=lf
# WHICH FILES ARE BINARY IS DECIDED BY BYTES, and `text=auto` above is what decides it: git looks
# for a NUL in the first 8000 bytes of the content. That the heuristic and a plain NUL scan agree
# over this whole tree, AND that the pin above really reaches every text file, is measured by
# `tools/test_repo_hygiene.py::test_git_decides_binary_by_bytes_and_pins_every_text_file_to_lf` --
# which asks `git check-attr` for the EFFECT, because everything else in that section reads the
# working tree and a working tree stays LF even after this pin is deleted. How many files each side
# holds today is in the round protocol, not here: a count in a comment is a second one to age.
# The lines below are the belt beside that brace, for the one direction that is expensive: a binary
# whose first 8000 bytes happen to hold no NUL would be line-ending converted and corrupted, while
# an over-pinned text file merely keeps its own bytes. They are an ENUMERATION, so both of their
# ends are measured rather than trusted -- an entry that names no binary kind in the tree, and a
# binary kind no entry names -- by
# `tools/test_repo_hygiene.py::test_every_binary_pin_names_a_kind_the_tree_has_and_every_kind_is_pinned`.
*.woff2 binary
*.png binary
